ttern).\n- Net-new dependencies on Node, pnpm, Vite, or React at runtime. Build-time bundling is fine.\n- Re-licensing UA. We treat UA as MIT inspiration; we vendor only what the license permits and credit the original.\n\n## Prior art in this repo\n\nTwo artifacts of this idea already exist; the plan must position itself against them:\n\n- **Earlier (approved) plan** at `i-want-to-do-this-for-entire-users-https-github-com-lum1104.md` shipped a deliberately smaller v1: a deterministic-edges-only `entire checkpoint graph` with JSON output and a CLI text view, no HTML viewer, no embeddings. It explicitly deferred the HTML viewer, web route, and embedding choice. *This plan re-opens those deferrals.*\n- **In-progress code**: a session on 2026-05-04 (visible in `cli/.entire/graph/sessions.json`) was building `cmd/entire/cli/graph/{builder,scanner,server,reviewer,query,openbrowser}.go`. None of it is on `main` today, but it indicates someone has already started a Go-side viewer prototype. Whoever picks up this plan should rebase against or reuse that work rather than start from zero.\n\nThe differences vs. the earlier approved plan are intentional: this plan ports UA's existing dashboard (rather than building a fresh viewer), commits to embedding a built JS bundle, and adds telemetry overlays UA cannot produce. The earlier plan's `entire checkpoint graph for <path>` text view stays as-is and becomes one of the explain/inspect surfaces here.\n\n## Proposal\n\n### Delivery\n\n**Single PR**, opened against `entireio/cli`. The change is structured as three sequential commits on one branch so reviewers can navigate it:\n\n1. `understand-go`: Go packages — graph builder, telemetry overlay, server, command wiring. The reviewable core.\n2. `dashboard-src`: vendored UA dashboard source under `cmd/entire/cli/understand/dashboard/src/` with the UA upstream commit hash recorded in `dashboard/UPSTREAM`.\n3. `dashboard-dist`: prebuilt `dashboard/dist/` bundle. Reviewers spot-check that `dist/` was reproducibly built from `src/`; CI enforces parity via `mise run dashboard:verify`.\n\nSplitting into multiple PRs is rejected: the Go side is meaningless without the embedded bundle, and the bundle-source-vs-dist pair has no value reviewed alone.\n\n### Command surface\n\nAdd `understand` as a 7th noun group. Justification per the CLI's promotion convention (>3 verbs): this group has 5. Verbs:\n\n```\nentire understand                   # bare: build graph + serve dashboard (the 90% path)\nentire understand build             # build/refresh .entire/graph/knowledge-graph.json only\nentire understand serve             # serve existing graph, open browser\nentire understand inspect <path>    # CLI text view of a file/symbol's provenance + telemetry\nentire understand diff              # impact preview vs. shadow-branch HEAD (uncommitted edits)\nentire understand onboard           # generate ordered tour, output to stdout or HTML\n```\n\n`entire understand` (bare) = `build` + `serve`. **Naming:** the verb is `inspect` (not `explain`) to avoid colliding with the existing top-level `explain` alias and `entire checkpoint explain`. The skill ecosystem (`/explain`) already maps to provenance lookups against the metadata branch and should not be re-pointed.\n\n### Architecture\n\nPer the CLI's repo convention (CLAUDE.md): noun-group command files live directly in `cmd/entire/cli/` as `<noun>_group.go` and `<noun>_<verb>.go`; supporting packages live in named subdirectories. Apply that here.\n\n```\ncmd/entire/cli/\n  understand_group.go         # Cobra group + bare-verb wiring\n  understand_build.go\n  understand_serve.go\n  understand_inspect.go\n  understand_diff.go\n  understand_onboard.go\n  understand/                 # supporting packages (not a command package)\n    graph/\n      builder.go              # Walks repo, produces nodes (file, dir, symbol) + edges (import, contains, cochange)\n      schema.go               # KnowledgeGraph struct, JSON marshaling — UA-compatible schema, additive `entire` field\n      incremental.go          # Re-analyze only changed files (UA pattern)\n      enrich.go               # Layer detection, framework registry — minimal Go reimpl of UA's heuristics\n    telemetry/\n      sessions.go             # Read .git/entire-sessions/ + entire/checkpoints/v1 via the existing checkpoint package\n      cochange.go             # Compute file co-change weights from per-checkpoint files_touched\n      agents.go               # Aggregate per-file agent footprint from CheckpointInfo.Agent + FilesTouched\n      prompts.go              # Pull prompt.txt → file mapping for provenance hover\n    server/\n      server.go               # net/http server, 127.0.0.1, token-gated, embeds dashboard\n      api.go                  # /api/graph, /api/file/:path, /api/checkpoint/:id, /api/diff\n      embed.go                # //go:embed dashboard/dist/**\n    dashboard/\n      UPSTREAM                # UA upstream commit hash + URL\n      dist/                   # Static bundle committed to repo (see \"Build\" below)\n      src/...                 # Vendored UA source for reproducible builds\n```\n\nThe graph package consumes existing types (`strategy.CheckpointInfo`, `session.State`, `agent/types`) and reads from `.git/entire-sessions/` and the `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch via the existing checkpoint store API — `ListCommitted(ctx)` is implemented on both `checkpoint.GitStore` (v1 storage) and `checkpoint.V2GitStore` (v2 storage), so the implementer should consume whichever the rest of the CLI is using at PR time and not pin a specific struct in this package's exported API. No new persistence layer.\n\n### Knowledge graph schema\n\nWe adopt UA's `knowledge-graph.json` shape (nodes/edges/layers/tours) so any UA-compatible viewer keeps working, then **extend** it with optional Entire-only fields. Each file/symbol node can carry:\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"id\": \"file:cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit.go\",\n  \"type\": \"file\",\n  \"label\": \"manual_commit.go\",\n  \"layer\": \"domain\",\n  \"lang\": \"go\",\n\n  // Entire-only fields (all optional, schema-additive):\n  \"entire\": {\n    \"checkpoint_count_30d\": 14,\n    \"agents_30d\": { \"claude-code\": 9, \"gemini-cli\": 3, \"factoryai-droid\": 2 },\n    \"last_checkpoint_id\": \"a3b2c4d5e6f7\",\n    \"last_session_id\": \"...\",\n    \"last_prompt_excerpt\": \"fix the prepush hook race\",\n    \"last_touched_at\": \"2026-…798 tokens truncated…ver-side proxy (we don't want the embedded JS bundle holding OAuth tokens directly). Defers to its own PR.\n\n### Serving HTML from the CLI\n\nMirrors UA's token-gated localhost pattern, but Go-native:\n\n1. `entire understand serve` picks a free port (default `127.0.0.1:0`), generates a 32-byte URL-safe token, prints `Dashboard: http://127.0.0.1:<port>/?token=<token>`.\n2. `net/http` server on `127.0.0.1` only — never binds to `0.0.0.0`. Token compared with `subtle.ConstantTimeCompare`.\n3. `//go:embed dashboard/dist` ships the prebuilt React bundle; static handler serves it. The `/api/*` handlers stream JSON from the in-memory graph + on-disk checkpoint metadata.\n4. Browser opens via `os/exec` using `open`/`xdg-open`/`rundll32`. Verified: no `openbrowser` / `browser.Open` helper currently exists in `cmd/entire/cli/`, so this PR adds a small one (≤30 LOC, in `understand/server/openbrowser.go`) — the in-progress prototype on the unmerged 2026-05-04 worktree appears to have one already; reuse it if it's salvageable.\n5. Server lifecycle: foreground by default with Ctrl-C handling; `--detach` flag for backgrounded serve. SIGINT/SIGTERM trigger graceful shutdown. No daemon, no PID file.\n\n### Build pipeline for the dashboard\n\nUA's dashboard is React + Vite + ELK + ReactFlow. We have two options; recommend the second:\n\n1. **Run `pnpm build` at user install time** — same as UA today. Cons: requires Node ≥ 22 + pnpm ≥ 10, slow first run, breaks offline installs. Rejected.\n2. **Build at CI time, embed dist into the Go binary** — `cmd/entire/cli/understand/dashboard/dist/` is committed (gitignored only the source `node_modules`). A `mise run dashboard:build` task drives `pnpm build` and writes into `dist/`. A `mise run dashboard:verify` task rebuilds and diffs against the committed `dist/`; CI runs `verify` to enforce `src/` and `dist/` stay in sync. **Recommended.**\n\n**Bundle-size budget:** measured against UA's current build before merge. Target: ≤2 MB compressed within the binary. Hard ceiling: 5 MB — above that, switch to download-on-first-run (cached under `~/.cache/entire/dashboard/<hash>/`). Empirical UA build size to be filled in by the implementer in the PR description.\n\n### Data flow on `entire understand`\n\n```\n1. Resolve repo root via paths.WorktreeRoot()\n2. Walk repo, respecting .gitignore + .understandignore (vendor UA's filter)\n3. For each file: language detect → parse imports/exports (per-language regex; parity with UA, no C deps)\n4. Build base graph (nodes + import/contains edges)\n5. Read .git/entire-sessions/*.json + entire/checkpoints/v1 via checkpoint.ListCommitted\n6. Aggregate per-file: agent counts, last prompt, last checkpoint, co-change edges\n7. Layer detection (architecture-analyzer heuristics ported from UA)\n8. Write .entire/graph/knowledge-graph.json (and ensure .entire/.gitignore includes graph/)\n9. Boot server, embed graph, open browser\n```\n\nIncremental: read `meta.json`, diff against `git rev-parse HEAD`, re-analyze only changed files; rebuild telemetry overlays in full (fast — they're just per-file counters).\n\n**v1 language scope:** Go, TypeScript/JavaScript, Python — same set UA ships with regex parsers. Other languages get included as plain file nodes (no import edges) but still receive full telemetry overlay; that's enough for the heatmap and provenance use cases. Adding a language is a regex module + test fixture, deferred unless a customer asks.\n\n**v1 scale target:** 5,000 checkpoints × 10k file nodes. Above that, fall through to the windowed view (last 30/90 days, configurable). Not solving \"render 50k nodes at once\" in v1.\n\n### LLM enrichment (optional, off by default)\n\nUA leans on an LLM for node summaries and tour generation. Native Entire users already have an authenticated agent (`text_generator_cli.go` resolves Claude/Gemini/etc.), so we expose `--enrich` to call out to whatever agent the user has configured for the small set of nodes that benefit. Off by default — the dashboard is fully usable on raw structure + telemetry alone.\n\n### Telemetry / privacy\n\n- Local-only by default. **Action item for the v1 PR:** extend `EnsureEntireGitignore` (in `cli/cmd/entire/cli/strategy/common.go`) to add `graph/` to the in-tree `.entire/.gitignore`. Without this the new artifact would land in user commits — same trap the prior plan caught.\n- Server binds to `127.0.0.1` only; token-gated with `subtle.ConstantTimeCompare`; never exposes prompts beyond the localhost socket.\n- The dashboard never holds an OAuth token. If a v2 cross-repo feature lands, it proxies through the local server.\n- `--enrich` (LLM node summaries) is opt-in and uses the user's already-configured agent CLI; does not transmit prompts to a third party.\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n- **Vendor UA wholesale and shell out to `pnpm`/Node.** Rejected: brings a TypeScript runtime dependency to every Entire user, breaks offline installs, fights the existing Go-only distribution model.\n- **Skill instead of command.** Could be authored as a Claude Code skill that calls into existing Entire CLIs. Rejected as the only deliverable: skills don't help Gemini/Cursor/Droid/Copilot users, and one of UA's headline use cases (`/understand-dashboard`) requires a long-running local server, which a skill can't own cleanly. A skill *wrapper* over the new command is fine as a follow-up.\n- **Ship telemetry overlays as a UA *plugin*** rather than a port. Tempting but UA has no plugin contract; we'd be patching the dashboard anyway, and we'd still depend on Node at runtime.\n- **Build a brand-new viewer from scratch.** Higher quality ceiling but ~5x the work; UA's React+ReactFlow+ELK stack is already battle-tested.\n\n## Pre-merge gates\n\nEach must be resolved before the v1 PR merges. These are the items that cannot be deferred to follow-ups.\n\n1. **License sign-off.** UA is MIT. We vendor `src/` + `dist/` under `cmd/entire/cli/understand/dashboard/`, retain UA's `LICENSE`, add a `NOTICE` crediting the original. *Owner: alisha@entire.io confirms with whoever owns OSS-license decisions for `entireio/cli` before the draft PR opens. The implementer should not assume MIT-vendoring is pre-approved.*\n2. **UA upstream pin.** Pin to a specific UA commit hash, recorded in `dashboard/UPSTREAM` (one line: `<sha>  https://github.com/Lum1104/Understand-Anything`). Renovate not enabled — upstream syncs are deliberate, after a manual diff review. *Owner: implementer picks a commit at PR-open time; default to UA's latest tagged release if there is one, otherwise the most recent green `main`.*\n3. **Bundle size measurement.** Build UA at the pinned commit; verify ≤2 MB compressed. Above 5 MB, switch to download-on-first-run (see Build pipeline). *Owner: implementer runs `pnpm install && pnpm build && du -sb dist/ | gzip -9 | wc -c` against the pinned commit and reports both raw and gzip sizes in the PR description; CI step `mise run dashboard:size-check` enforces the 5 MB ceiling on every change.*\n4. **Gitignore update.** `.entire/.gitignore` must include `graph/` before the PR adds artifact-writing code. *Verified 2026-05-04: today's `.entire/.gitignore` lists `tmp/`, `settings.local.json`, `metadata/`, `current_session`, `logs/` — `graph/` is missing, so this is real, not theoretical.* This update goes in the first commit (Go core), before any code that writes to `.entire/graph/`.\n5. **Schema back-compat fixture test.** Same requirement carried over from the prior approved plan: a JSON fixture in `cmd/entire/cli/understand/graph/testdata/golden_v1.json` that v1 produces and a test (`TestGraphSchema_BackwardsCompatible`) that asserts every UA-required field plus every documented `entire.*` field is present. Future versions must keep producing a graph that this fixture still validates against. Without this, the schema-versioning promise to v2 features is empty.\n\n## Risks & Open Questions (deferred)\n\n- **Onboarding ranking weights.** Rank-normalized additive scoring is the default. Real-world tuning happens once the dashboard is in customers' hands.\n- **Default activity window.** Defaulting to 30 days. Configurable via flag and persisted in `.entire/settings.json`. Revisit if telemetry shows users always tweaking it.\n- **Co-change scaling beyond 5k checkpoints.** Out-of-scope for v1; switch to count-min sketch / top-K heap when a customer hits the cap.\n- **Time-machine slider data layout.** Pre-computing per-checkpoint graph snapshots is expensive; on-demand re-analysis at past commits is slow. Either approach is a v2 design problem, not a v1 blocker.\n\n## Decision\n\nApproved v1 scope:\n- 5 enrichments shipped in v1 (agent footprint, prompt-anchored provenance, co-change edges, hot-path onboarding, live diff impact).\n- Time-machine slider and cross-repo search hop-out deferred to v2 follow-up PRs.\n- Verb name is `inspect`, not `explain`, to avoid colliding with `entire checkpoint explain`.\n- Single PR with three sequential commits (Go core → dashboard src → dashboard dist).\n- All five pre-merge gates resolved before the PR merges.\n\n### Next steps (in order)\n\n1. **alisha@entire.io** confirms license owner sign-off (Gate 1).\n2. **Implementer** fetches the in-progress 2026-05-04 worktree (`cli/.entire/graph/sessions.json` references a session that built `cmd/entire/cli/graph/{builder,scanner,server,reviewer,query,openbrowser}.go`) and triages reusable code under the new `cmd/entire/cli/understand/` layout.\n3. **Implementer** picks a UA upstream commit, runs the bundle-size measurement (Gate 3), opens a draft PR with commits in the order Go core → dashboard src → dashboard dist.\n4. **Reviewers** spot-check that `dashboard/dist/` was reproducibly built from `dashboard/src/` (CI's `mise run dashboard:verify` does this automatically; manual sanity check on first review).\n5. Merge after gates 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 are green.\n\nThis plan is final. Open questions in \"Risks & Open Questions\" are deliberately deferred — they do not block the v1 PR.\n\n---\n\nBegin.\n"}}
